---
// Code signing policy for the Windows desktop installers. Its name, the roles
// and the privacy statement follow SignPath Foundation's conditions
// (signpath.org/terms). Once the application is accepted, add their credit line
// at the top: "Free code signing provided by SignPath.io, certificate by
// SignPath Foundation" (with links to about.signpath.io and signpath.org).
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { REPO_URL, RELEASES_URL } from '../consts';

const WORKFLOW_URL = `${REPO_URL}/blob/main/.github/workflows/desktop.yml`;
const MAINTAINER_URL = 'https://github.com/evank-dev';
const ORG_PEOPLE_URL = 'https://github.com/orgs/sidewinder-labs/people';
---

<Base
	title="Code signing policy — Sidewinder Flow Studio"
	description="How the Sidewinder Flow Studio desktop installers are built and signed, who approves each release, and what the app sends over the network."
>
	<section class="section">
		<div class="wrap">
			<div class="prose">
				<span class="eyebrow">Desktop edition</span>
				<h1>Code signing policy</h1>

				<p>
					Signing the Windows installers lets Windows show who published them and confirm they haven't been
					changed since. Signing is being set up with SignPath Foundation; until it is in place, the Windows
					installers are not signed and Windows SmartScreen may warn about them.
				</p>

				<h2>What is signed</h2>
				<p>
					Only software built from the
					<a href={REPO_URL}>Sidewinder Flow Studio repository</a>, which is open source under AGPL-3.0:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li>the Windows installers attached to each <a href={RELEASES_URL}>GitHub release</a>
						(<code>…_x64-setup.exe</code> and <code>…_x64_en-US.msi</code>);</li>
					<li>the programs built from the repository inside them: <code>sfs-desktop.exe</code> (the app window)
						and <code>sfs-backend.exe</code> (the data engine).</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					The installers also contain unmodified open-source libraries from other projects, such as the
					Python runtime, pandas, PyArrow, DuckDB and Polars. These are included as their projects publish
					them and are not signed by us. Nothing else is signed under this policy: in particular, no
					commercial add-on is ever part of the signed software.
				</p>

				<h2>How a release is built and signed</h2>
				<ol>
					<li>A version tag is pushed to the repository.</li>
					<li>GitHub Actions builds the installers from that tag, in the
						<a href={WORKFLOW_URL}>public build workflow</a>, and runs the smoke tests on the result.</li>
					<li>The signing request is approved by hand, by an approver (below), for that release only.</li>
					<li>The signed installers are attached to a draft release, checked, and then published.</li>
				</ol>
				<p>
					No installer is built or signed on a personal computer. Every signed file carries the product name
					“Sidewinder Flow Studio” and the release's version number in its properties.
				</p>

				<h2>Team and roles</h2>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Committers and reviewers</strong>: members of the
						<a href={ORG_PEOPLE_URL}>Sidewinder Labs organisation</a> on GitHub. Changes from anyone else
						(pull requests) are reviewed by a member before they are merged.</li>
					<li><strong>Approvers</strong>: owners of the organisation, who approve each signing request.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					The project currently has one maintainer, <a href={MAINTAINER_URL}>evank-dev</a>, who holds all three
					roles. Everyone in these roles uses multi-factor authentication on GitHub and on the signing service.
				</p>

				<h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
				<p>
					This program will not transfer any information to other networked systems unless specifically
					requested by the user or the person installing or operating it.
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Your projects, data, settings and saved passwords stay on your computer.</li>
					<li>The one automatic connection is the <strong>update check</strong> when the app starts: it
						downloads the public list of the latest release from GitHub and sends nothing about you or your
						data. Turn it off by setting the environment variable <code>SFS_NO_UPDATE_CHECK=1</code>.</li>
					<li>The app connects to a database, or to an AI model provider, only after you add that connection
						yourself, and only to the address you give.</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>Questions and reports</h2>
				<p>
					To report a problem with a signed file, or anything that looks wrong in a release, open an issue in
					the <a href={`${REPO_URL}/issues`}>repository</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
